# Futrob design contract

Read [design.md](../../design.md) before designing, implementing or reviewing UI.
It owns visual rules, typography, tokens, navigation, screen patterns, states and
verification. Keep design decisions there rather than introducing another contract.

- Reuse current text primitives / `typography.*` and semantic tokens. Token values
  live in `packages/ui-tokens/src`; regenerate CSS through its package scripts when
  values change. `packages/ui/src/tokens.css` is generated.
- Both theme aliases use Grafito + Lima. Follow the documented responsive and touch
  behavior rather than introducing a separate palette or typography scale.
- For pages, sections, KPIs and empty states, use the matching repo creation skill.
  Read the [shared composition reference](../skills/references/design-composition.md)
  for Inicio and the closest current page. Recency alone does not make legacy UI canonical.
- Keep compositions in their owning app and reusable primitives in the UI package.
  For existing components needing stories, use [add-story](../skills/add-story/SKILL.md).
- Web uses [futrob-stylex](../skills/futrob-stylex/SKILL.md). Native uses its own
  primitives in `apps/mobile/src/ui` and shared tokens; preserve platform boundaries.
- Verify relevant states in stories and the requested user flow. Report build,
  interaction and visual evidence separately; a successful build is not visual proof.
